<title>USA: Orbital unit wins $18.9 mln Taiwan pact.</title>
<headline>Orbital unit wins $18.9 mln Taiwan pact.</headline>
<dateline>DULLES, Va. 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Orbital Sciences Corp said its Fairchild defense division had won an $18.9 million contract from Taiwan.</p>
<p>Under the contract, the division will equip Taiwan's air force with mission planning and data transfer systems products over the next two years, Orbital said.</p>
<p>Orbital said the mission planning system provides a fully integrated flight planning and threat analysis capability that allows a fighter pilot to &quot;rehearse&quot; a mission prior to actual flight.</p>
<p>The data transfer system integrates the mission planning data with the aircraft's computer, it said.</p>
<p>The two electronic products reduce ground planning time and minimize in-flight  pilot workload, it said.</p>
